What’s new
6 November 2026 — Version 0.1.5. The Observatory is now also published from the project’s GitHub account, and the recommended citation on the About page now gives that address. The results are unchanged.
6 November 2026 — Version 0.1.4. Aligned the Municipal typology of family farming page with the current version of Manuscript 1, with no change to the numerical results. The page now states the two hypotheses, explains that they were fixed after an exploratory analysis of the same data and declares that Hypothesis 1 is not supported in the form stated. The oblimin and promax rotations now have the same standing, and caveats on Hypothesis 2, suppression and the silhouette have been added. On the Agricultural Census tenure data and agrarian reform page, corrected the reference to “low” tenure in the T3 label.
5 November 2026 — Version 0.1.3. Corrected the ranks of tied municipalities in the ranking charts, which now match those on the profiles and cards, and the wording of the area card on this page, which refers to the area of establishments rather than of the state.
5 November 2026 — Version 0.1.2. Added an English version of the website, available via the flags in the menu bar, and listed the project team in About.
23 October 2026 — Version 0.1.1. Revised the page text to use scientific language, with no change to figures, sources or results.
19 October 2026 — Version 0.1. First version for the project team, covering:

the 141 municipalities, with 34 indicators and IBGE symbols displayed;
the indicator sources: 2017 Agricultural Census data on family farming, INCRA/SIPRA, SEEG 13 and the 2006–2017 dynamics;
the municipal typology from Manuscript 1 (k = 5, provisional labels);
Census tenure data and agrarian reform;
emissions and deforestation by type, with the official PRODES series and the correction note;
the three pilot areas, with identifying details only, and the six specific objectives;
the literature, limited to metadata, with 115 references on carbon, markets and ESG and 38 studies compared for SO4;
the data for download, with a data dictionary, sources and licences.
